 "notes": [
  "All sources are CC0 and human-made (recorded or made with synths by named authors, all published 2010-2020). Evidence is in ../sfx_src/<source_pack>/SOURCE.txt.",
  "Only ffmpeg trimming, fades, level and format conversion were applied. Nothing was synthesised.",
  "All files share the same PEAK level, so they are not loudness-balanced: use suggested_mix_db as a starting volume_db per sound in the game.",
  "Variation files are <name>_1.ogg, <name>_2.ogg ...; pick one at random and add a small random pitch (about +/-5%).",
  "Style rule: physical things (weapons, monsters, doors, coins, rocks) are recorded foley; feedback sounds (UI, hearts, hurt, jingles) are chiptune.",
  "See the \"gaps\" list for sounds that are weak or approximate."
 ],
 "gaps": [
  "IMPORTANT: every sound was chosen from file names, the authors' descriptions, measurements and spectrogram pictures. Nobody has listened to this set yet. Do one listening pass in the game before release.",
  "bomb_fuse: WEAK. It is a 0.5 s hiss burst (source file is just called \"noise\"), not a real burning fuse. A real fuse sound on OpenGameArt (themightyglider, \"Simple Fuse Sound\") was rejected because it is derived from a Freesound file whose licence could not be checked (freesound.org refused the connection).",
  "curse_whisper (optional): WEAK. A slowed ghostly breath with no whispered words. No CC0 human-made whisper was found.",
  "boss_die: a second troll roar take (it falls in pitch and dies away), not a dedicated death cry. Layer it with explosion_1 in the game.",
  "enemy_die_big: only the longest take of the normal enemy death set. The deep CC0 monster deaths that were found are almost pure bass and would be nearly silent on phone speakers.",
  "player_hurt / player_die: retro synth sounds, not a human voice. No CC0 human grunt could be confirmed without listening.",
  "stairs_descend: a retro falling transition sweep, not footsteps on stone stairs.",
  "cursed_item_pickup: a falling chiptune run (mirror of item_pickup), not a dark atmospheric sting.",
  "player_shoot_magic: only 2 variations and they have different timbres.",
  "torch_fire_loop (optional): loop made with a crossfade; mostly low rumble, so it will be quiet on phone speakers.",
  "victory_sting: harpsichord, while the other jingles are chiptune. The same jingle exists as a square-wave version in sfx_src/fupi_win_jingle/original/winjingle.zip (WinSquare.wav) if one style is wanted.",
  "chest_open: short wooden lid thump with no creak."
 ],
